From: Project Luma <project-luma@local>
Subject: [PATCH] simple: respect the sensor's minimum analogue gain step

The S5KKD1SP front sensor exposes integer 1x gain steps. Simple IPA derives a
generic minimum adjustment by dividing the whole gain range by 100, producing
0.63x here. The first dark-scene correction therefore requests 6.63x, but the
helper's integer gainCode() correctly quantizes that back to 6. Every following
stats frame starts from 6x again, so AE never raises gain after exposure time
reaches its frame-duration limit.

Make the minimum adjustment at least the real-gain difference between adjacent
sensor codes. This preserves proportional convergence for fine-grained sensors
while guaranteeing forward progress for coarsely quantized controls.

--- a/src/ipa/simple/soft_simple.cpp
+++ b/src/ipa/simple/soft_simple.cpp
@@ -6,5 +6,6 @@
  */
 
+#include <cmath>
 #include <chrono>
 #include <stdint.h>
 #include <sys/mman.h>
@@ -245,11 +246,16 @@ int IPASoftSimple::configure(const IPAConfigInfo &configInfo)
 	if (camHelper_) {
 		context_.configuration.agc.againMin = camHelper_->gain(againMin);
 		context_.configuration.agc.againMax = camHelper_->gain(againMax);
 		context_.configuration.agc.again10 = std::max(context_.configuration.agc.againMin, 1.0);
 		context_.configuration.agc.againMinStep =
 			(context_.configuration.agc.againMax -
 			 context_.configuration.agc.againMin) /
 			100.0;
+		if (againMax > againMin)
+			context_.configuration.agc.againMinStep = std::max(
+				context_.configuration.agc.againMinStep,
+				std::abs(camHelper_->gain(againMin + 1) -
+					 camHelper_->gain(againMin)));
 		if (camHelper_->blackLevel().has_value()) {
 			/*
